\f7\b\fs36 \cf2 2. THE RECEIVER (Welder Side)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The receiver converts the wireless signal into a real analog voltage (0-10V) for amperage control. It uses two electromechanical relays: one to start the welding arc, and another to isolate the welder's potentiometer ground when resting, eliminating any signal noise.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl276\sa240\partightenfactor0
